# comment 00197030 kwlnInitPS2Systems: IOP bring-up. InitRpc/InitIopHeap/CdInit/CdMmode(2); reboot IOP with rom0:UDNL cdrom0:\LIB31\IOPRP310.IMG;1 (retry loop); SyncIop; re-init; T0 time base + INTC9 handler; 15x sceSifLoadModule (SIO2MAN,SIO2D,PADMAN,DBCMAN,MC2_S1,LIBSD,CRI_ADXI "sdinit=0 spucore=1",SDRDRV,MODHSYN,MODMSIN,MODSESQ,SKSOUND,SKHSYNTH x2,SKSESQ "maxtrack=16\0maxentry=16") each retried while <0; H_Pad_Init; H_Memcard_Init; saves main thread id to gp-0x4C28. ev: 12 s1
# comment 00196fe0 INTC 9 (TIM0) handler: when T0_MODE.OVFF, add 0x10000 to the 64-bit tick counter at gp-0x4C58 (T0 runs at BUSCLK/16). ev: 12 s4.3
# comment 0019d320 INTC 2 (VBLANK_START) handler installed by kwlnInstallVBlankStartHandler: sync;ei; returns 0 if GS_CSR.FIELD else -1. ev: 12 s4.4
# comment 0019d360 AddIntcHandler(2, kwlnVBlankStartHandler, 0) + EnableIntc(2); handler id at gp-0x6BA8. Called from kwlnInitRenderer. ev: 12 s4.4
# comment 0010c5f0 Per-frame resource-manager pump (from kwlnRootUpdateShowRasterTask): walks sResrcMan request list, issues H_Cdvd_Request, and when a file is loaded sets the thread control block (gp-0x4DC0) and WakeupThread(H_Resman_ThreadProc). ev: 12 s4.1
# comment 0010cce0 EE->IOP memory copy for sound banks: {src,dst,size,0} at g_sndcomSifDmaReq, FlushCache, sceSifSetDma, busy-wait sceSifDmaStat. Asserts (h_sndcom.c:263) if the DMA could not be queued. ev: 12 s2.3
# comment 00506088 libsifcmd public sceSifSetDma: when sifcmd is initialised routes through sceSifSetDmaInternal (adds 16-byte sync packet), else raw syscall. Used by libpad _send_to_iop, sceSdTransToIOP, H_Sndcom_CopyToIop, CRI DTR. ev: 12 s2.3
# comment 00506110 libsifcmd isceSifSetDma (interrupt-context variant of 0x506088). ev: 12 s2.3
# comment 00505fc0 Builds the SIF DMA list (<=32 entries) plus a trailing 16-byte packet (header dword_7BDD00 -> IOP cmd buffer dword_966A60) and issues (i)sceSifSetDma. FLIRT had this as sceSifInitCmd (wrong; the real init is 0x506148). ev: 12 s7
# comment 00506148 sceSifInitCmd: sifcmd init -- cmd buffer 0x966A58, handlers change_addr/set_sreg, AddDmacHandler(5, sceSifCmdIntrHdlr), EnableDmac(5), exchanges IOP cmd-buffer address via SIF regs 0x80000000/0x80000001 and cmd 0x80000002. ev: 12 s2.2
# comment 0051dc70 SK HSYNTH Bind: 64-byte block {0x1000000, 0, a1..a6} sent via sceSdRemote(1,0x9100,blk,64). Game: Bind(3,-1,iopHd,hdSize,spuAddr,bdSize)->id and Bind(5,-1,id,0)->id2. ev: 12 s2.3
# comment 0051dd48 SK HSYNTH Unbind: block {0x1000000, 1, kind, id}. ev: 12 s2.3
# comment 0051ddf0 SK SESQ Bind: block {0x4000000, 0, a1..a4}. Game: Bind(0,-1,iopSq,sqSize)->id3; Bind(5,hsynId2,id3)->control handle. ev: 12 s2.3
